WEBVTT

00:03:03.990 --> 00:03:05.920
A photo shoot on the beach...

00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:08.740
It's been so long since I've been to the beach.

00:03:08.740 --> 00:03:10.850
Why is Meroko in such high spirits?

00:03:11.250 --> 00:03:14.390
Ignoring that... did your manager
get in touch with you?

00:03:14.390 --> 00:03:14.950
Yep.

00:03:15.330 --> 00:03:17.120
If we're going to the beach...

00:03:17.120 --> 00:03:18.500
...it'll be good for my health.

00:03:18.500 --> 00:03:19.920
I'm really happy about it.

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:20.670
Is that so?

00:03:20.670 --> 00:03:21.130
Yep!

00:03:21.550 --> 00:03:22.900
Ah! That's right!

00:03:22.900 --> 00:03:23.270
Hmm?

00:03:23.590 --> 00:03:25.770
I wonder if I should bring my swimsuit.

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:27.490
Hey.

00:03:27.490 --> 00:03:29.690
Don't forget about the Shinigami oath.

00:03:29.700 --> 00:03:31.760
Geez... I know that already.

00:03:32.600 --> 00:03:33.760
Are you sure?

00:03:49.370 --> 00:03:51.780
Wow! The air feels so different.

00:03:52.620 --> 00:03:53.690
Ooshige-san.

00:03:53.690 --> 00:03:55.740
Is it okay if I take a little walk?

00:03:56.460 --> 00:03:58.060
Come back soon, okay?

00:03:58.250 --> 00:03:59.210
Okay!

00:04:00.050 --> 00:04:02.990
Hey, hey! Where's she going, 
leaving us behind like that?! {Hey, hey! No?}

00:04:02.990 --> 00:04:05.360
I want to go to the beach too!

00:04:07.140 --> 00:04:08.960
Oh! Here it is!

00:04:13.680 --> 00:04:15.350
This isn't the beach, you know!

00:04:15.350 --> 00:04:16.390
It doesn't matter!

00:04:28.280 --> 00:04:29.630
A trip...

00:04:29.630 --> 00:04:32.470
Not even a fever could ruin this, right? {}

00:04:33.680 --> 00:04:34.280
Yep!

00:04:34.280 --> 00:04:37.200
Wow! This feels good!

00:04:38.160 --> 00:04:40.210
Yo-re-i-ho! {Echo}

00:04:39.960 --> 00:04:41.710
Yo-re-i-ho! {Echo}

00:04:41.710 --> 00:04:43.330
Yo-re-i-ho! {Echo}

00:04:43.500 --> 00:04:45.040
Yo-re-i-ho! {Echo}

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:47.670
It feels so good to be able to use my voice so loudly.

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:55.640
That girl's so simplistic.

00:04:55.640 --> 00:04:56.470
Takuto!

00:04:56.470 --> 00:04:57.560
Hmm? What is it?

00:04:57.560 --> 00:04:59.080
Pay attention!

00:04:59.080 --> 00:05:01.640
You <i>do</i>  remember what you told me last night, right?

00:05:01.640 --> 00:05:02.540
Last night?

00:05:02.820 --> 00:05:07.000
You told me that we can't allow her to meet
the person who will change her fate.

00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:09.210
I know about that already.

00:05:09.210 --> 00:05:11.680
Besides... you're the one who should be paying attention...

00:05:11.680 --> 00:05:14.070
We didn't come here on a picnic.

00:05:14.660 --> 00:05:16.160
I'm <i>so</i>  sorry!

00:05:21.540 --> 00:05:22.120
Ow.

00:05:23.090 --> 00:05:25.360
Didn't we say to wait for us? {"you" doesn't make sense, so replaced by "we"}

00:05:25.360 --> 00:05:27.380
What are you going to do if something happens?

00:05:27.380 --> 00:05:28.590
What do you mean by "something"...?

00:05:29.130 --> 00:05:30.320
By something, I mean...

00:05:31.050 --> 00:05:31.630
...like...

00:05:31.970 --> 00:05:34.050
If the fact that you're really twelve years old was revealed...

00:05:34.050 --> 00:05:36.010
There's no way something like 
that is going to happen. {}

00:05:36.020 --> 00:05:36.610
Look.

00:05:36.610 --> 00:05:38.510
As long as I'm like this, there's no way I'll be found out.

00:05:39.850 --> 00:05:41.460
Mitsuki-chan!

00:05:43.020 --> 00:05:44.790
It's about to begin, so...

00:05:44.790 --> 00:05:45.940
...come back over here!

00:05:46.320 --> 00:05:47.540
Okay!

00:05:51.870 --> 00:05:53.700
So then, shall we begin?

00:05:54.080 --> 00:05:55.570
Please do your best.

00:05:56.370 --> 00:05:58.640
Those are some cute stuffed animals.

00:05:58.640 --> 00:06:00.140
You're <i>Full Moon-san,</i> right?

00:06:00.140 --> 00:06:00.760
Yes!

00:06:00.760 --> 00:06:03.080
They're my very important friends!

00:06:03.210 --> 00:06:04.600
I see.

00:06:04.600 --> 00:06:07.080
I'm Takeda from Monthly SuperStar.

00:06:07.080 --> 00:06:08.540
It's a pleasure to be working with you.

00:06:09.510 --> 00:06:11.510
The Monthly SuperStar?

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:18.700
Mitsuki-chan.

00:06:20.440 --> 00:06:21.790
Mitsuki-chan!

00:06:22.310 --> 00:06:23.020
Y-Yes!

00:06:23.350 --> 00:06:24.230
Introduce yourself.

00:06:24.230 --> 00:06:26.280
I-I'm<i> Full Moon!</i>

00:06:26.610 --> 00:06:27.980
It's a pleasure to be working with you.

00:06:27.980 --> 00:06:29.400
Please excuse her.

00:06:29.400 --> 00:06:31.360
That's just how she is.

00:06:31.360 --> 00:06:34.240
She's much more adorable than I thought she'd be.

00:06:34.240 --> 00:06:34.950
Um...

00:06:34.950 --> 00:06:36.860
You're a high school student, right?

00:06:36.860 --> 00:06:39.010
Yes! I'm sixteen years old!

00:06:39.010 --> 00:06:40.960
My blood type is A!

00:06:40.970 --> 00:06:42.290
My hobby is reading!

00:06:42.660 --> 00:06:44.160
My favorite color is blue!

00:06:44.420 --> 00:06:46.370
Yep, yep, that's the way.

00:06:46.370 --> 00:06:48.210
All that practicing is paying off. {continuous tense sounds more appropriate here, even though japanese language doesn't have that}

00:06:48.210 --> 00:06:49.130
You think so?

00:06:49.300 --> 00:06:50.420
In my spare time...

00:06:50.420 --> 00:06:53.200
...I enjoy sitting in my room daydreaming.

00:06:53.200 --> 00:06:54.510
I guess you could say that...

00:06:54.510 --> 00:06:56.630
...I'm the type of person who takes pride in being independent.

00:06:58.850 --> 00:07:00.700
You're quite an interesting person, huh?

00:07:01.120 --> 00:07:01.890
I suppose...

00:07:05.770 --> 00:07:06.310
Ah.

00:07:06.730 --> 00:07:07.850
Excuse me.

00:07:07.850 --> 00:07:09.520
I have to leave for a bit, so...

00:07:09.520 --> 00:07:11.000
...I'll leave everything to you.

00:07:11.000 --> 00:07:11.520
Okay.

00:07:11.520 --> 00:07:12.270
That's fine.

00:07:13.860 --> 00:07:16.380
This is your first interview, right?{}

00:07:16.380 --> 00:07:17.450
Good luck!

00:07:17.450 --> 00:07:19.150
Ah. Okay.

00:07:21.740 --> 00:07:24.310
Hmm... so then, <i>Full Moon-san...</i>

00:07:24.310 --> 00:07:27.890
...how long have you wanted to be a singer?

00:07:27.890 --> 00:07:28.410
Yes!

00:07:28.750 --> 00:07:30.210
Since I was ten years old!

00:07:31.670 --> 00:07:34.210
You're quite sure of yourself.

00:07:34.210 --> 00:07:37.420
Did something occur that caused this to happen?

00:07:37.420 --> 00:07:37.970
Eh?

00:07:41.390 --> 00:07:43.310
It's to meet Eichi-kun, right?{}

00:07:44.140 --> 00:07:45.680
But, that's...

00:07:46.920 --> 00:07:47.490
Ah?

00:07:48.070 --> 00:07:49.020
What's wrong?

00:07:49.020 --> 00:07:50.100
Ah. It's nothing.

00:07:50.100 --> 00:07:51.730
Um...

00:07:52.070 --> 00:07:55.880
I want lots of people to listen to my songs!

00:07:55.880 --> 00:07:57.070
I see.

00:07:57.070 --> 00:07:58.240
Let's see...

00:07:58.580 --> 00:08:00.860
Is there a singer you're trying to be like?

00:08:00.860 --> 00:08:01.360
Eh?

00:08:01.910 --> 00:08:02.990
Shoot!

00:08:02.990 --> 00:08:04.200
We didn't practice this! {This was a bit tricky, because we use Practise as verb, and practice as noun, but I guess I am going to stick with "American Practice" here. Likewise I left practicing before as it was.}

00:08:06.330 --> 00:08:07.330
What's wrong?

00:08:07.330 --> 00:08:08.350
Don't you have one?

00:08:08.350 --> 00:08:09.710
W-Well...{}

00:08:10.380 --> 00:08:12.880
I like everyone who sings.

00:08:14.680 --> 00:08:16.760
My question was pretty insignificant, huh?

00:08:16.760 --> 00:08:19.630
So then... what kind of foods do you like?

00:08:20.720 --> 00:08:23.300
Taiyaki and our school's Shrimp Pilaf.

00:08:23.480 --> 00:08:24.140
Ah?!{}

00:08:24.140 --> 00:08:25.100
The school's...?!{He is obviously surprised!}

00:08:26.690 --> 00:08:27.520
Dummy...

00:08:27.980 --> 00:08:29.180
School food?

00:08:29.690 --> 00:08:32.580
<i>Full Moon-san,</i> you're a high school student, aren't you?{removed dash between full moon}

00:08:32.580 --> 00:08:34.320
Your school provides meals?

00:08:34.320 --> 00:08:35.610
T-That's not what I meant!

00:08:35.610 --> 00:08:36.670
Um...

00:08:36.670 --> 00:08:38.650
The Shrimp Pilaf from back in elementary school...

00:08:38.650 --> 00:08:41.280
...I still can't forget how much I loved it!

00:08:43.790 --> 00:08:44.830
<i>Full Moon-san...</i>

00:08:44.830 --> 00:08:47.330
...you're really a grade school student, aren't you?

00:08:52.550 --> 00:08:54.000
I'm just kidding.

00:08:54.000 --> 00:08:55.610
Please don't worry about it.

00:08:55.610 --> 00:08:56.590
Ah. Okay.

00:09:00.600 --> 00:09:03.300
It looks like we didn't practice hard enough.

00:09:03.300 --> 00:09:06.180
The things you told her to say were totally irrelevant!

00:09:06.180 --> 00:09:08.270
It'll be a problem if they get published.

00:09:08.270 --> 00:09:09.220
What's that?!

00:09:30.380 --> 00:09:30.870
Ah!

00:09:38.680 --> 00:09:40.210
Why don't you try walking around a little?

00:09:40.590 --> 00:09:41.470
O-Okay.

00:09:47.960 --> 00:09:50.390
Well, try posing by lifting your hand? {Missing line}

00:09:50.390 --> 00:09:50.990
Eh?

00:09:51.100 --> 00:09:52.350
Oh. Okay!

00:09:53.940 --> 00:09:54.810
Look here...

00:09:54.810 --> 00:09:56.400
Can't you make it look more natural?!

00:09:56.400 --> 00:09:56.860
Eh?

00:09:59.360 --> 00:10:00.440
I'm sorry.

00:10:03.200 --> 00:10:06.950
Even if you say that... she's just an amateur, after all.

00:10:06.950 --> 00:10:08.660
Can't you be a tad more considerate?

00:10:09.120 --> 00:10:11.080
Look at the water this time, then.

00:10:11.080 --> 00:10:13.590
Pretend that you're gazing into the distance at the scenery.

00:10:13.590 --> 00:10:14.670
O-Okay.

00:10:20.840 --> 00:10:22.170
That's no good! No good!

00:10:22.170 --> 00:10:24.390
I can't take a picture of you like that!

00:10:24.590 --> 00:10:25.530
Break time!

00:10:26.390 --> 00:10:27.220
Man...

00:10:50.830 --> 00:10:51.870
Sorry.

00:10:51.870 --> 00:10:56.500
Our boss likes to work himself into a trance,
so his clientèle have to fit his style. {spacing issue}

00:10:56.500 --> 00:10:57.360
Don't worry about it.

00:10:57.360 --> 00:11:00.390
I should be apologizing because 
she's so inexperienced.

00:11:00.390 --> 00:11:02.120
Well, it's gotten cloudy...

00:11:02.120 --> 00:11:03.550
...let's take a little break.

00:11:09.220 --> 00:11:10.220
Mitsuki-chan.

00:11:12.600 --> 00:11:13.810
I'm sorry.

00:11:13.810 --> 00:11:15.020
Don't fret over it.

00:11:15.200 --> 00:11:16.730
It's okay to just do things at your own pace.

00:11:17.770 --> 00:11:18.520
But...

00:11:20.440 --> 00:11:22.000
Do you want to take a walk?

00:11:22.280 --> 00:11:23.870
Since we have some time now...

00:11:25.190 --> 00:11:25.880
Come on.

00:11:26.450 --> 00:11:28.200
You'll feel better.

00:11:30.570 --> 00:11:31.330
Okay.

00:11:33.950 --> 00:11:36.250
What is that dummy so down for?

00:11:36.250 --> 00:11:37.540
You're wrong.

00:11:37.540 --> 00:11:40.320
She just needs to get some fresh air after 
the cameraman made her feel incompetent!{needs not went}

00:11:40.320 --> 00:11:41.290
If it were me...

00:11:41.290 --> 00:11:43.640
...I'd show him just how charming I could be!

00:11:43.640 --> 00:11:44.800
I see.

00:11:44.800 --> 00:11:47.420
That girl isn't showing her charm.

00:11:47.420 --> 00:11:48.100
Huh?{}

00:11:48.720 --> 00:11:50.550
That girl's charm?

00:11:50.680 --> 00:11:51.800
Geez!

00:11:51.800 --> 00:11:52.890
What do you mean by charm?!

00:11:52.890 --> 00:11:54.890
I was talking about myself!

00:11:54.890 --> 00:11:56.720
What does this have to do with you?

00:11:56.720 --> 00:11:58.270
It doesn't matter! Geez.

00:11:58.270 --> 00:12:00.190
I won't let you see her anymore!

00:12:00.770 --> 00:12:01.860
Hey! You!

00:12:01.860 --> 00:12:02.730
What'd you do?!

00:12:02.730 --> 00:12:04.530
Hey Meroko, get this off!

00:12:04.530 --> 00:12:06.440
Where am I?! {Cannot be Overlap with what Takuta was saying from the previous line}

00:12:06.860 --> 00:12:08.740
Hey! What is this?! {}

00:12:08.990 --> 00:12:09.950
The keyword is...

00:12:11.070 --> 00:12:12.530
Female high school students?

00:12:12.530 --> 00:12:13.490
What the...?

00:12:13.490 --> 00:12:15.200
Can I find them in a place like this?

00:12:34.930 --> 00:12:36.800
I'm kinda tired...

00:12:46.530 --> 00:12:49.350
If they find out that I'm really twelve years old...

00:12:49.350 --> 00:12:50.360
...I wonder what would happen.

00:12:51.040 --> 00:12:53.640
They might even cancel my debut.

00:12:55.210 --> 00:12:56.590
If that were to happen...

00:12:56.590 --> 00:12:58.330
...I wouldn't be able to meet Eichi-kun.

00:13:01.420 --> 00:13:02.640
I have to do my best...

00:13:07.130 --> 00:13:10.710
So that I can find Eichi-kun.

00:13:11.590 --> 00:13:12.600
That's right!

00:13:12.600 --> 00:13:14.430
That's why I want to become a singer!

00:14:33.060 --> 00:14:33.840
Ah!{}

00:14:37.930 --> 00:14:39.240
Ah? Um...

00:14:39.240 --> 00:14:40.430
Who are you?

00:14:40.430 --> 00:14:41.080
Eh?

00:14:41.310 --> 00:14:43.830
We heard a really, really beautiful voice, so...

00:14:43.830 --> 00:14:45.640
...we thought we should come and check it out.

00:14:45.640 --> 00:14:48.580
It was just someone singing and being carefree... we were surprised!

00:14:48.580 --> 00:14:49.860
Ah. I'm sorry.

00:14:51.230 --> 00:14:52.860
There's nothing to apologize for.{'s added}

00:14:52.860 --> 00:14:55.360
But you really do have a pretty voice.

00:14:56.280 --> 00:14:58.660
Hey, why are you in a place like this?

00:14:59.780 --> 00:15:00.950
In a place like this...?

00:15:01.410 --> 00:15:02.330
Could it be that...

00:15:02.330 --> 00:15:05.290
...you're one of those people who believes in the <i>Sixteen Year Old Hill?</i>

00:15:05.750 --> 00:15:07.500
The <i>Sixteen Year Old... Hill?</i>

00:15:07.500 --> 00:15:08.250
The <i>Sixteen Year Old... Hill?</i>

00:15:08.250 --> 00:15:09.960
What? That's not it?

00:15:09.960 --> 00:15:10.940
Man...

00:15:11.920 --> 00:15:13.160
This hill...

00:15:13.160 --> 00:15:17.130
It's rumored around these parts that if on your...

00:15:17.320 --> 00:15:19.990
...sixteenth birthday, when you come here...

00:15:19.990 --> 00:15:23.370
...there's a myth that you'll get a boyfriend.

00:15:23.370 --> 00:15:26.650
And... today's A-chan's birthday.

00:15:26.650 --> 00:15:27.600
Yep!

00:15:27.730 --> 00:15:30.440
That's why we all came here today.

00:15:48.580 --> 00:15:50.800
Just where did that girl run off to?

00:15:50.800 --> 00:15:53.420
And I don't see any female high school students around here.

00:15:53.630 --> 00:15:56.480
Ah! This cellphone is new, isn't it?{cellphone space removed}

00:15:56.480 --> 00:15:57.660
Eh? What?

00:15:57.840 --> 00:15:59.600
You can play games on this, right?

00:15:59.600 --> 00:16:00.480
Games?

00:16:00.760 --> 00:16:01.850
You don't know about that?

00:16:01.850 --> 00:16:02.430
Yeah.

00:16:03.640 --> 00:16:04.360
Look.

00:16:04.890 --> 00:16:06.180
Ah. You really can.

00:16:06.410 --> 00:16:08.000
So there are, from time to time...

00:16:08.000 --> 00:16:11.650
...high school students who don't know how to use cellphones.

00:16:11.900 --> 00:16:13.650
Are you talking about... me?

00:16:13.650 --> 00:16:15.020
It can't be that...

00:16:15.020 --> 00:16:16.970
...you never receive any e-mail, right? {or text messages, still up on the air about this one}

00:16:16.970 --> 00:16:18.330
Huh? E-mail?{M changed to m}

00:16:18.330 --> 00:16:19.580
Just as I thought.

00:16:19.580 --> 00:16:22.070
I was wondering if that was possible.

00:16:25.920 --> 00:16:27.000
Ah, that's right!

00:16:27.330 --> 00:16:29.120
Speaking of which, how old are you?

00:16:29.120 --> 00:16:30.100
Twelve years old.

00:16:32.080 --> 00:16:32.900
Ah! {this was indeed Kouyama Mitsuki}

00:16:32.900 --> 00:16:34.120
No way! {not sync}

00:16:34.120 --> 00:16:37.130
I thought that you'd be around sixteen, like me.

00:16:37.130 --> 00:16:38.170
Ah! That's right!

00:16:38.170 --> 00:16:38.800
Yeah, yeah.

00:16:38.800 --> 00:16:40.260
I'm actually sixteen!

00:16:40.470 --> 00:16:41.900
That's right.

00:16:41.910 --> 00:16:44.600
No matter how you look at it, she doesn't look twelve at all.

00:16:44.790 --> 00:16:47.200
Man... she had me going there!

00:16:55.570 --> 00:16:58.520
Hey, do you want me to teach you how to use your e-mail? {or text, I might flip a coin to see if I should change it}

00:16:58.900 --> 00:16:59.360
Okay! {}

00:16:59.630 --> 00:17:01.570
Let's exchange addresses then. {on second thought, I'll stick to e-mail}

00:17:04.120 --> 00:17:06.990
Ah! She was in a place like this.

00:17:06.990 --> 00:17:08.880
Aren't those female high school students?!

00:17:08.880 --> 00:17:09.810
This is bad.

00:17:10.330 --> 00:17:11.790
Hey! You girls!

00:17:11.790 --> 00:17:12.320
Ah?

00:17:12.710 --> 00:17:14.830
Get away from Mitsuki!

00:17:20.010 --> 00:17:22.260
Meroko? What are you doing?

00:17:22.260 --> 00:17:23.470
My job!

00:17:23.470 --> 00:17:24.100
Eh?

00:17:26.760 --> 00:17:28.270
Ah. Meroko.

00:17:29.440 --> 00:17:31.210
What are you doing here?

00:17:32.230 --> 00:17:32.740
Huh?

00:17:32.980 --> 00:17:34.480
The keyword of <i>danger</i>  in there...

00:17:34.480 --> 00:17:36.700
...it says female high school students!

00:17:36.700 --> 00:17:37.320
It really does.

00:17:37.320 --> 00:17:37.940
That's why...

00:17:37.940 --> 00:17:39.750
I have to separate them!

00:17:41.010 --> 00:17:41.490
Ah!

00:17:41.490 --> 00:17:42.400
Meroko.

00:17:42.400 --> 00:17:42.990
What?

00:17:43.410 --> 00:17:44.280
This.

00:17:45.530 --> 00:17:47.620
Excluding those with loose socks?

00:17:48.950 --> 00:17:51.210
Ugh. What was that wind just now?

00:17:51.620 --> 00:17:52.750
It tingles...

00:17:54.880 --> 00:17:56.420
No way...

00:17:58.920 --> 00:18:00.720
Ah! It's already this late!

00:18:01.750 --> 00:18:03.890
Well, we have to go back now.

00:18:03.890 --> 00:18:04.400
Eh?

00:18:04.400 --> 00:18:05.470
Ah. Okay.

00:18:05.470 --> 00:18:06.680
Later, then.

00:18:06.680 --> 00:18:07.770
Later.

00:18:07.770 --> 00:18:09.100
I hope we meet again.

00:18:09.100 --> 00:18:10.270
Next time, we'll use e-mail.

00:18:10.680 --> 00:18:11.280
Okay!

00:18:18.110 --> 00:18:19.430
Thank you!

00:18:20.610 --> 00:18:21.620
You know...

00:18:21.620 --> 00:18:24.230
...I'm going to be debuting as a singer soon!

00:18:29.990 --> 00:18:31.000
That's great!

00:18:32.140 --> 00:18:33.660
We'll cheer for you!

00:18:34.420 --> 00:18:35.790
Thank you!

00:18:45.510 --> 00:18:46.510
Geez...

00:18:46.840 --> 00:18:50.010
Because of you, I had to fly all over the place.{comma replacing full stop}

00:18:50.220 --> 00:18:50.810
Hey.

00:18:50.970 --> 00:18:51.720
See... about me... {she says watashi, but "I... they told me" makes no sense}{shani: changed it}

00:18:51.720 --> 00:18:54.140
They told me that I look like I'm sixteen.

00:18:54.730 --> 00:18:55.920
Oh <i>really?!</i> {Meroko is kinda yelling here, the interrobang makes more sense}

00:18:55.920 --> 00:18:57.810
That's good to know!

00:18:57.810 --> 00:18:59.230
Hey, Takuto.

00:18:59.700 --> 00:19:02.240
I really look like I'm sixteen years old now! {I added the now because I think Mitsuki was alluding to what she was desperately saying in episode 1 "do I look like I'm sixteen?", in which Takuto replied "no, not really".}

00:19:02.240 --> 00:19:03.800
Well, of course.

00:19:04.070 --> 00:19:06.700
That's why the truth hasn't been discovered.

00:19:08.620 --> 00:19:09.690
I see.

00:19:09.690 --> 00:19:10.920
That's how it is.

00:19:12.660 --> 00:19:13.120
Ah.

00:19:13.860 --> 00:19:15.520
Where did you go?

00:19:15.520 --> 00:19:17.630
I was about to call you.

00:19:17.630 --> 00:19:19.210
You know, um...

00:19:19.590 --> 00:19:20.920
...the <i>Sixteen Year Old Hill.</i>

00:19:21.120 --> 00:19:22.050
What's that?

00:19:22.960 --> 00:19:24.100
It's just...

00:19:24.510 --> 00:19:28.440
...what the local high school students around here call that hill. {Mitsuki says local high school students later on, consistency}

00:19:28.440 --> 00:19:31.100
If you go on that hill on your sixteenth birthday...

00:19:31.100 --> 00:19:34.480
...they believe that you'll find a boyfriend. {kinda needs a little editing work}{shani: i am okay with this}

00:19:35.980 --> 00:19:39.020
That's what the local high school students said.

00:19:43.400 --> 00:19:44.990
You're really quite interesting. {do people really say amazingly anymore, I dunno}

00:19:44.990 --> 00:19:46.700
You explained it so well.

00:19:46.840 --> 00:19:47.570
Hey!

00:19:47.570 --> 00:19:48.660
We're starting!

00:19:48.910 --> 00:19:49.700
O-Okay!

00:19:49.700 --> 00:19:52.030
Then... do your best, Mitsuki-chan.

00:19:52.030 --> 00:19:52.960
Good luck.

00:19:53.160 --> 00:19:53.650
Okay!

00:20:08.260 --> 00:20:08.890
Ah.

00:20:08.890 --> 00:20:10.050
That's a good pose.

00:20:10.050 --> 00:20:11.430
You're growing into a woman, aren't you?

00:20:11.430 --> 00:20:13.350
Thank you very much!

00:20:14.890 --> 00:20:16.850
Mitsuki's so...beautiful...

00:20:17.190 --> 00:20:18.120
Hmm...{}

00:20:18.120 --> 00:20:18.960
Huh?

00:20:18.960 --> 00:20:20.100
Takuto!

00:20:20.100 --> 00:20:20.520
Hmm?

00:20:22.290 --> 00:20:23.020
What's that?

00:20:23.020 --> 00:20:26.260
You're the one who said she was "beautiful" in the first place, right?

00:20:31.700 --> 00:20:32.500
And then...

00:20:32.780 --> 00:20:37.460
I realized that it was unreasonable and that there was no need for me to try to be an adult.

00:20:38.000 --> 00:20:38.690
That's right.

00:20:39.290 --> 00:20:42.990
I think that you should stay just the way you are, too.

00:20:43.150 --> 00:20:43.600
Yep!

00:21:11.240 --> 00:21:13.410
Girls are so... mysterious.

00:21:13.410 --> 00:21:13.950
Eh?

00:21:15.280 --> 00:21:17.660
Just when you think they're being childish...

00:21:18.200 --> 00:21:20.000
...they suddenly look so grown up.{}

00:21:20.160 --> 00:21:20.580
Eh?!

00:21:21.170 --> 00:21:22.880
I-I wonder if that's true?

00:21:23.000 --> 00:21:24.560
I hit it right on the nose, didn't I? {I think that's how the idiom goes}

00:21:24.560 --> 00:21:26.550
What are you thinking about right now, Mitsuki-chan?

00:21:26.550 --> 00:21:28.280
Nothing at all!

00:21:29.920 --> 00:21:30.720
Geez...

00:21:30.720 --> 00:21:32.600
I said nothing at all!

00:23:06.270 --> 00:23:07.020
Wah!

00:23:07.020 --> 00:23:08.190
What's with that girl?

00:23:08.190 --> 00:23:10.230
Where is she planning on taking me?

00:23:10.230 --> 00:23:10.690
Geez...

00:23:10.690 --> 00:23:11.860
Takuto, you oaf!

00:23:11.860 --> 00:23:15.910
How could you let someone see you talk while you were a stuffed animal?!

00:23:15.910 --> 00:23:17.200
I couldn't help it!

00:23:17.200 --> 00:23:18.740
She kept going on and on so foolishly.

00:23:18.740 --> 00:23:21.200
Because she kept saying "I can't record...", that's why!

00:23:21.200 --> 00:23:22.660
You should have just run away!{run, not ran}

00:23:22.660 --> 00:23:23.750
That's true, but...

00:23:23.970 --> 00:23:24.960
Wait a minute.

00:23:24.960 --> 00:23:25.920
This girl is...

00:23:26.540 --> 00:23:28.580
Next time on Full Moon wo Sagashite:

00:23:28.580 --> 00:23:30.210
The Long Day in the Studio.
